# RootForge OS — optional desktop layer for the Termux/Android variants
# Victorious Framework | Origin Source Labs
#
# Installed only when build-rootfs.sh is passed --with-x11. Kept separate
# from the base list because it roughly triples the tarball: the base rootfs
# is a headless toolchain, and most users of it never want a desktop.
#
# The X server itself is NOT here. It lives on the Termux side as the
# Termux:X11 companion app plus its `termux-x11` launcher — this list is only
# the client-side desktop that connects to it.
#
# XFCE rather than GNOME: GNOME needs systemd/logind and a compositor stack
# that neither PRoot nor a chroot on Android's kernel provides. XFCE runs
# fine as a plain X client with no session manager underneath it.

xfce4
xfce4-terminal
xfce4-panel
xfce4-session
xfce4-settings
xfdesktop4
xfwm4
thunar

# X client libraries and the utilities a desktop session actually calls out
# to. dbus-x11 provides dbus-launch, which xfce4-session needs.
dbus-x11
x11-xserver-utils
x11-utils
xterm

# Fonts — without these the desktop renders as boxes.
fonts-dejavu-core
fonts-liberation2

# A file manager and text editor are the two things people immediately reach
# for in a desktop session; the rest they install themselves.
mousepad
